# client-facing-prefixes.txt — skills whose output a customer sees, so rewrites need
# a high-taste model and an orchestrator read, never a cheap-model draft.
# One skill DIRNAME PREFIX per line, matched with startswith (so `email-` catches
# `email-sequence`, `email-marketing`, ...). Blank lines and # comments are ignored.
#
# This file MUST NOT be empty — assign_client_facing.py errors on an empty list.
# Library with no client-facing skills? Keep the dummy prefix below: nothing starts
# with `zzz-none-`, so every skill is flagged client_facing=false and the stage passes.
zzz-none-

# Delete the dummy above and uncomment/extend once you know the library, e.g.:
# carousel-
# email-
# content-
# copywriting
# brandkit
# humanizer
